# CMPG 325 – Milestone 1: Client Design Review

## Project Information

**Project ID:** CMPG325-2026-075  
**Client ID:** CI-075  
**Organisation:** Mammonto Building Projects (Taung)  
**Industry:** Construction  

## Client Requirements

The network is designed for Mammonto Building Projects (Taung), a construction organisation. The assigned IPv4 addressing block is 10.32.0.0/16, and the assigned networking challenge is Wireless LAN integration and coverage.

The building is heritage-listed, therefore no new cabling may be installed through external walls. The network also accommodates the requested eight additional staff members in one department without requiring a complete network redesign.

## Physical Topology

The physical topology consists of an edge router, main switch, access switch, wireless access points, end-user devices and a shared server or service device where required.

## Logical Topology

The logical network is separated into the following VLANs:

| VLAN | Name | Subnet |
|---|---|---|
| 10 | ADMIN | 10.32.10.0/24 |
| 20 | PROJECT | 10.32.20.0/24 |
| 30 | FINANCE | 10.32.30.0/24 |
| 40 | STAFF-WIFI | 10.32.40.0/24 |
| 99 | MANAGEMENT | 10.32.99.0/24 |

## IP Addressing

Each VLAN uses a /24 subnet with the first usable address assigned as the default gateway. The Project/Technical subnet provides sufficient capacity for the requested eight additional staff members.

## Wireless LAN

Wireless LAN integration and coverage is the assigned networking challenge. Wireless access points provide connectivity for staff and mobile devices while taking the heritage-building cabling restriction into consideration.

## Repository

The GitHub repository serves as the working portfolio for the project and contains the Milestone 1 documentation, with the same project continuing through Milestone 2 and the final submission.
